{"about_you":"Software engineer with a new job and a long commute, which disrupts eating — often skips lunch or grabs a gas-station sandwich, and tends to log only 3 items a day. Training is consistent (4 sessions/week) and logging is excellent (21-day streak). Goal is a lean gain from 158 to 172 at ~0.5 lb/week, but currently under-eating (~2,085 kcal avg) and drifting down — needs practical ways to add volume, especially at lunch.","assessment":"The engine is running, but the fuel is short. Training and logging are rock-solid (21-day streak), but every single day this week landed **under** the 2,650 floor — 1,951 to 2,200 kcal. The scale agrees: you're down ~0.6 lb/week and the trend sits at 160, when a lean gain to 172 needs it moving **up** ~0.5 lb/week. This isn't a willpower problem — it's a calorie gap. Close it and the gain starts.","calorie_max":2850,"calorie_min":2650,"changelog_note":"Flagged under-eating: 6/6 days below the 2,650 floor and trend drifting down 0.6 lb/week — held targets, shifted insights to closing the calorie gap.","headline":"Off track for lean gain — eating too little to grow","insights":[{"body":"All 6 days this week: 1,951–2,200 kcal, all below your 2,650 floor. That's a ~500+ kcal daily gap. Pick one meal to make bigger or add a 4th item — closing this is the whole game.","title":"You're eating under every day","tone":"watch"},{"body":"Down 0.6 lb/week, trend at 160. A lean gain needs it climbing ~0.5 lb/week. More food is literally the path back — this reverses fast once you hit range.","title":"Trend is drifting down, not up","tone":"watch"},{"body":"Three weeks straight, no gaps. This consistency is exactly why we can see the problem clearly and fix it — don't lose it.","title":"21-day logging streak","tone":"win"},{"body":"You've slipped to ~100 g the last few days vs the 145 g target. A shake or a bigger protein portion at dinner covers both the protein gap and the calorie gap at once.","title":"Protein's a little light lately","tone":"nudge"},{"body":"You're skipping or grabbing a gas-station sandwich on the commute. A planned lunch — even a second sandwich or a packed meal — is the simplest 600 kcal to add.","title":"Lunch is the easy win","tone":"nudge"}],"protein_target":145,"strategy":"Lean gain needs a small, steady **surplus** — roughly 200–300 kcal/day above maintenance. Right now you're averaging ~2,085, which is below your floor and causing a slow slide down instead of up.

**The fix is volume, not restriction:** you're consistently logging only 3 items a day and skipping lunch on the commute. Adding one more eating occasion — or just bigger portions at the two meals you already eat — gets you into range easily.

I'm holding the range at 2,650–2,850 and protein at 145 g; the targets are right, the execution needs to hit them. The goal every day: **don't finish below 2,650.**"}

{"assessment":"**Off track, but easy to fix.** Your trend is **160 lb**, up 2 from 158, but it's now **drifting down ~0.6 lb/week**. That's the opposite of the +0.5 lb/week we want.

The cause is clear. Every logged day this week landed at **1,951–2,200 kcal**, about **450–700 under the 2,650 floor**. Protein ran **95–115 g** against 145. Training isn't the problem. The food gap is.","protein_target":145,"calorie_max":2850,"goal_summary":"Lean gain to 172 lb","about_you":"Software engineer who started a new job with a long commute. Eats 3 times a day with no snacks: a coffee drink for breakfast, a grab-and-go lunch (often a gas station sandwich), then dinner. Lunch used to be skipped. Trains about 4x/week and is a very consistent logger (21-day streak). Goal is a lean gain to 172 lb.","timeframe":"~0.5 lb/week, roughly 6 months","strategy":"**Keep the range at 2,650–2,850 and protein at 145 g.** The targets are right. Your intake just hasn't reached them yet. At about 2,075/day you're slowly losing, so maintenance looks to be around 2,350–2,400. Adding roughly 300 more on top of that gives the lean +0.5 lb/week.

**The fix is one more eating slot, not bigger meals.** You eat only 3 times a day. Add one portable 500–600 kcal snack with 30–40 g protein for the commute, and you'll close most of the gap.","changelog_note":"Targets unchanged; intake is running ~600 kcal under the floor and the trend turned down, so the focus shifted to adding a commute snack and more protein.","headline":"Eating ~600 under — add a commute snack to resume gaining","calorie_min":2650,"insights":[{"title":"21-day streak","tone":"win","body":"Three straight weeks of logging. That's exactly why the gap is so easy to spot. And you're up 2 lb from 158 overall, so the base is there."},{"title":"Under the floor every day","tone":"watch","body":"Each logged day this week was 1,951–2,200 kcal, below the 2,650 floor, and the trend slipped to -0.6 lb/week. Eating under the range stalls the gain. It's not a bonus."},{"title":"Pack a commute snack","tone":"nudge","body":"You eat just 3 items a day. Add one ~550 kcal snack to your bag: a protein shake plus a banana and peanut butter, or Greek yogurt with granola. That alone puts you near 2,650."},{"title":"Protein ~40 g short","tone":"nudge","body":"You're averaging about 104 g against 145. Upgrade the gas station lunch: add a protein milk or jerky alongside the sandwich (+20–30 g). Then aim for 50 g at dinner with extra meat in the pasta."},{"title":"Water at 17 of 79 oz","tone":"nudge","body":"Bring a bottle on the commute and finish it before you get to work. That's a quick third of your goal done before lunch."}]}

{"about_you":"Sam is working toward 145 lb at a relaxed pace of about 0.5 lb/week, starting from 162 lb. Sam trains at the gym about 3 times a week (45-minute Legs, Back, and Chest sessions) and logs food consistently, with a 28-day streak. Meals are mostly simple and repeatable: overnight oats, turkey sandwiches, and chicken stir fry. Weekends and occasional big days run higher on calories, and protein tends to fall short.","assessment":"**Holding steady, which is a normal plateau, not a failure.** Trend is 158 lb (started at 162), so you're 4 lb in and 13 lb from the 145 goal. Calories have landed inside the 1,500–1,650 range on most days this week, with one-off highs on Thu (1,700) and Sat (1,751) and Yesterday (1,711). Protein is the weak spot: 85–97 g, averaging about 91 g against a 100 g target. Logging streak is 28 days.","calorie_max":1650,"calorie_min":1500,"changelog_note":"Protein target held at 100 g and calorie range held at 1,500–1,650; added a protein-gap nudge and a weekend high-day watch, since calories are mostly in range but protein averages about 91 g.","goal_summary":"Reach 145 lb at a relaxed ~0.5 lb/week","headline":"Steady at 158 lb, 4 lb down from 162, on a 28-day logging streak","insights":[{"body":"Four weeks of consistent logging is exactly the habit that makes this work. Keep the streak going.","title":"28-day logging streak","tone":"win"},{"body":"Trend is 158 lb, holding steady. That's a normal plateau after 4 lb of progress. Stay the course; the trend usually moves again within a few weeks.","title":"Weight is holding, not failing","tone":"win"},{"body":"You averaged about 91 g against the 100 g target, with a low of 85 g on Saturday. Adding one lean protein per day closes most of that gap.","title":"Protein is short most days","tone":"nudge"},{"body":"Saturday (1,751) and Yesterday (1,711) ran over the 1,650 ceiling. Most other days sat inside the range. Plan one lighter meal on weekends.","title":"High-calorie days pull the average up","tone":"watch"}],"protein_target":100,"strategy":"**Keep the calorie range at 1,500–1,650 kcal.** The floor keeps you fueled for three gym sessions a week; the ceiling keeps the ~0.5 lb/week pace on track. Tighten the weekend and high-day spread, since the 1,700+ days are what's pushing the average up.

**Close the protein gap.** Target 100 g daily. Add roughly 10 g per day by swapping one carb-heavy item for a lean protein (Greek yogurt, eggs, or extra chicken). Protein also helps hold muscle while you're in a deficit.

**Water:** you're at 17 of 81 oz today. Front-load bottles before lunch so you're not catching up at night.","timeframe":"by spring, at a relaxed ~0.5 lb/week"}

{"about_you":"Marketing desk job; work starts at 6am, so training is two short gym sessions a week (Legs/Back, Chest/Shoulders). Lactose intolerant: avoids milk, yogurt, and soft cheese, so protein comes from meat, eggs, tofu, or lactose-free or plant-based options. Logs food daily with a 21-day streak. Goal is 145 lb at a relaxed, sustainable pace; currently 159 lb, down from 162.","assessment":"**On track.** Intake has sat inside the 1,550–1,700 kcal range on every logged day this week (1,580–1,720; one day, Sat, ran 20 kcal over the soft ceiling). Protein is the gap: 71–85 g/day against a 105 g target. Trend is 159 lb, down 3 lb from the 162 lb start, at a gentle 0.3 lb/week. Training dropped to two short sessions a week, and the 21-day logging streak is excellent.","calorie_max":1700,"calorie_min":1550,"changelog_note":"Protein target held at 105 g; reframed the protein gap as the main lever now that Greek yogurt is out (lactose intolerance), and updated training to two sessions a week.","goal_summary":"Reach 145 lb at a relaxed pace (~0.5 lb/week target)","headline":"Steady loss, in range, 159 lb and falling","insights":[{"body":"Daily protein has been 71–85 g against a 105 g target. Today's latte carries only 20 g. Add one high-protein anchor per meal, such as a shake, eggs, or extra chicken or turkey, to close the gap without adding much calorie.","title":"Protein is running about 25 g short","tone":"watch"},{"body":"Every logged day this week landed between 1,580 and 1,720 kcal, with the one overage only 20 kcal over the ceiling. That consistency is what drives the trend, so keep it up.","title":"Calories are in the range, day after day","tone":"win"},{"body":"With no milk, yogurt, or soft cheese, reach for lactose-free milk, a whey isolate or pea protein shake, tofu, tempeh, or eggs. Oat milk lattes are fine but add little protein, so pair them with protein at breakfast.","title":"Lactose-free protein swaps","tone":"nudge"},{"body":"Down 3 lb from 162 to 159 at about 0.3 lb/week. That is a healthy rate for a relaxed goal, with the goal of 145 lb reached around September 2027. No need to push harder.","title":"Pace is gentle and sustainable","tone":"win"},{"body":"With the 6am start, two 30-minute gym sessions a week (most recently Legs and Back) are a workable floor. Protect those two slots and keep the logging streak going, now at 21 days.","title":"Two sessions still count","tone":"nudge"}],"protein_target":105,"strategy":"**Keep the calorie range as is.** Intake is landing where it should and the pace is sustainable, so no need to change it.

**Protein is the lever to pull.** Greek yogurt is off the table now (lactose intolerant), so protein needs new anchors: chicken, turkey, eggs, tofu or tempeh, lactose-free dairy or a whey/pea protein shake. Aim to add roughly 25–30 g at one meal, for example a protein shake in the morning instead of a plain latte.

**Training:** two 30-minute sessions a week is a real, workable floor with a 6am start. Keep them consistent rather than adding more.","timeframe":"by September 2027 at current pace"}
